<title>CANADA: Negligible frost seen on Canada's east Prairies-EC.</title>
<headline>Negligible frost seen on Canada's east Prairies-EC.</headline>
<dateline>WINNIPEG 1997-08-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>No significant frost was reported on Canada's Prairie grain belt Sunday or Monday mornings, an Environment Canada meteorologist said.</p>
<p>&quot;I wouldn't be surprised if some farms around Dauphin (Manitoba) saw frost (Monday) but it definitely wasn't widespread, just a few patches,&quot; meteorologist Mark Gerlyand said.</p>
<p>Wasagaming, in western Manitoba's Riding Mountain National Park, saw a low of 0 Celsius (32 F) Sunday morning, he said.</p>
<p>Alberta and Saskatchewan's grainbelts saw overnight lows Sunday and Monday that were well above freezing, he said.</p>
<p>Alberta's Peace River Valley saw lows of four to five Celsius.</p>
<p>((Gilbert Le Gras, Winnipeg Reuters bureau 204 947 3548))</p>
